  "provenance": [
    {
      "source_type": "manufacturer-pdf",
      "source": "Topps official checklist PDF: MLB2401-2024ToppsSeries1BBChecklistV1.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-07",
      "covers": "Series 1 (#1-350) and its inserts",
      "notes": "This document prints no RELIC marker at all, only INSERT, AUTOGRAPH RELIC and AUTOGRAPH, so five relic programmes fell through to the default kind and were filed as relics from the Series 2 document instead: Major League Material Cards, 1989 Topps Baseball Relics, City Connect Swatch Collection, In The Name Relics and Cut Signatures. It also misspells its own header as \"Topps Reverence Autogaph Patch Cards\", corrected to match Series 2. Card #219 is interleaved in the PDF text and repaired deterministically to Christian Encarnacion-Strand, Cincinnati Reds, Rookie. One non-card section skipped: Social Media Follow Back Redemption Cards."
    },
    {
      "source_type": "manufacturer-pdf",
      "source": "Topps official checklist PDF: MLB2402-2024ToppsBBSeries2ChecklistFinal.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-07",
      "covers": "Series 2 (#351-700) and its inserts",
      "notes": "Cards #413, #424 and #481 print a league where the team would go — American League, Major League Baseball, National League — which is why those values are in teams.json. American League was added for this set; no card in the 2025 or 2026 checklists prints it. One non-card section skipped: Social Media Follow Back Redemption."
    },
    {
      "source_type": "community",
      "source": "Baseball Card Pedia, 2024 Topps",
      "source_url": "https://baseballcardpedia.com/index.php/2024_Topps",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-07",
      "covers": "the Traded Gimmicks variation; the Kevin Hart Gimmicks variation; the Kayfabe Rookies variation; the two factory set checklists",
      "notes": "Neither Topps checklist lists these two cards, in any section: #50 appears only as Juan Soto of the San Diego Padres. Both are variations of base cards — #50 shows Soto after his trade to the Yankees, and #250 shows Shohei Ohtani where the base card is Mookie Betts, a different player on the same number. Team abbreviations NYY and LAD are expanded to the forms Topps prints elsewhere in this set. Kevin Hart Gimmicks is eighteen cards with the comedian photoshopped into the foreground, every one a Phillie, and all eighteen verify against base.csv on number, name and team. Two claims about them are not recorded. That source says they are exclusive to Series One packs, but twelve of the eighteen carry Series 2 numbers and this set's Series 1 is #1-350 exactly, so the claim cannot be right as stated. And each is serial numbered to 52 — a joke about Hart's height — which has nowhere to go, because print_run belongs to a parallel and this is a variation checklist. Kayfabe Rookies is #697-700 with Jackson Holliday, Jackson Chourio, Jackson Merrill and Wyatt Langford where the base cards are Jordan Diaz, Gio Urshela, Sean Bouchard and Jose Altuve — four different players on four existing numbers, the same shape as 2026's Short Print Rookies. Topps prints no name for them and no checklist lists them, so the name is the one that source gives its section; teams and the RC designation are taken from where this set prints those players elsewhere. Trading Card Database describes the same four as the base factory set versions of those numbers, which is consistent and is why the 582 Montgomery Club entry says they are on the base checklist. Factory Set Rookie Variations is five cards in the retail factory set: #60, #141 and #553 keep their base players, while #697 and #698 carry Jackson Holliday and Jackson Chourio over Jordan Diaz and Gio Urshela. Trading Card Database lists factory set variations at #697-700 instead, adding Merrill and Langford and dropping the three lower numbers, so the two sources disagree on the extent; the five named here are what this source states. Factory Set All-Stars is five inserts in the All-Star Game factory set, numbered 1-5 of their own — base #1-5 are Ronald Acuña Jr., the Padres team card, Endy Rodríguez, Logan Webb and Owen White — so it declares no varies."
    }
  ],
